      Recounts


    Recounts are conducted by the Board of Elections under Rhode Island General Laws 17-19-37.1, 17-19-37.2, and 17-19-37.3.
All recounts are held at the Board of Elections offices at 2000 Plainfield Pike, Cranston, RI 02921. All recount requests must be original and signed by the candidate, and notarized. Please include the full name, address, contact information, and related office being sought in the request. Requests will not be accepted if faxed or e-mailed. To request a recount, we recommend you do so with the following form: Recount Request Form
Additional information on recounts may be obtained here in the Guide to Election Recounts.
 
All recounts are open to the public






























